    "explicit_limitations": [
      "The 19.03x peak throughput speedup occurs on the 2x4090D testbed whose Intel Xeon 8368Q CPU lacks AMX, degrading KTransformers to AVX2; on AMX-equipped Xeon 8470Q (5090), the throughput ratio narrows to <=2.30x, and reserved KTransformers (KT) keeps lower TTFT and TPOT than Rimuru on Qwen3-30B.",
      "Compared with resident SGLang and vLLM, Rimuru lowers queueing TTFT (-63% to -99%) via higher admission concurrency but incurs noticeably higher decode TPOT (~200-250 ms vs. <90 ms) due to on-demand PCIe weight transfers.",
      "CUDA Graph is disabled across all end-to-end evaluations in Section 8; runtime comparison with piecewise CUDA Graph enabled against CUDA-Graphed resident serving engines is not measured.",
      "Algorithm 1 relies on an offline static hotset ranking {H_l} and empirical routing probabilities {p_l} rather than online drift adaptation, and expert_offload_limit (EOL) still requires per-deployment tuning to balance KV headroom against burst-recovery reload latency.",
      "Evaluations cover ShareGPT prompts across three Qwen3/Qwen3.5 MoE models without variance bars or 1M-context stress benchmarks; Rimuru inherits vLLM base non-weight memory footprint (e.g., Triton GDN autotuning OOM on Qwen3.5-122B), and no public code repository link is cited in the preprint."
    ]
